text Elements that have a  content attribute ensure that the cryptographic nonce is only exposed to script (and not to side-channels like CSS attribute selectors) by taking the value from the content attribute, moving it into an internal slot named , exposing it to script via the  interface mixin, and setting the content attribute to the empty string. Unless otherwise specified, the slot's value is the empty string.
