link implementation-defined https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#implementation-defined
text Set a minimum value that most often results in the resources being loaded before they intersect the viewport under normal usage patterns for the given device.
text The typical scrolling speed: increase the value for devices with faster typical scrolling speeds.
text The current scrolling speed or momentum: the UA can attempt to predict where the scrolling will likely stop, and adjust the value accordingly.
text The network quality: increase the value for slow or high-latency connections.
text User preferences can influence the value.
text It is important  that the  not leak additional information. For example, the typical scrolling speed on the current device could be imprecise so as to not introduce a new fingerprinting vector. success
